      "writtenOn": "2020-04-30T19:37:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yup, we can keep trying to discover the cable nDiscoverIdentityCount times.\n\nIf PD 2.0 times out, it doesn\u0027t hurt to re-set to PD 2.0.  I wouldn\u0027t expect a cable to hit this condition too often normally (it\u0027s a cable... how much else does it really have to do besides reply to SOP\u0027 discovery?) but the worst-case would be that we only have PD 2.0 discovery information for what was actually a misbehaving PD 3.0 partner.  Since PD 3.0 provides us with collision avoidance, we should hopefully not often time out with an actual PD 3.0 port partner.",
      "parentUuid": "3f488b73_b33fcdb9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4185,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 4187,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1f139d55152a79671ffceb34b6e86e88a7c0bb8a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
